<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-sequences-and-series" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Sequences and Series</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      Think back to the games you enjoyed as a child, perhaps you played hide and seek, football, dodgeball, skipping rope, or a ball throwing game with friends.
    </p>
    <p>
      Have you ever noticed that these games often involved counting or following a particular order? 
    </p>
    <p>
      For example, when playing hide and seek, did you search for hiding places randomly, or did you usually begin with the nearest or most obvious places before moving to the next ones? When dividing players into two football teams, did you count, “<m>1, 2, 1, 2, …,</m>” so that all those who counted <m>1</m> formed one team and those who counted <m>2</m> formed the other? If three teams were needed, did the counting become “<m>1, 2, 3, 1, 2, 3, …,</m>” with everyone who counted the same number joining the same team?
    </p>
    <p>
      In ball throwing or skipping games, how did players know whose turn came next? Was it by chance, or did everyone follow an agreed pattern?
    </p>
    <p>
      <term>What do all these activities have in common?</term>
    </p>
    <p>
      Although they may seem like ordinary childhood games, each one relies on recognising and following a rule or pattern that allows us to predict what comes next. Mathematics studies these patterns and provides a language for describing them. In this topic, you will discover that the ideas behind many games you have played all your life are closely connected to the mathematical concepts of sequences and series.
    </p>
    <p>
      In this chapter, we will explore sequences and series. A sequence is an ordered list of numbers that follow a specific pattern, while a series is the sum of the terms of a sequence. We will learn how to identify different types of sequences, such as arithmetic and geometric sequences, and how to find their sums. Additionally, we will discuss real-life applications of sequences and series in various fields.
    </p>
  </introduction>

